  "title": "Sizing Up Market Expectations for the FOMC",
  "summary": "Tomorrow afternoon, all eyes will once again be focused on the Federal Reserve. Although market expectations do not favor a hike, there is a persistent perception that one could occur. As meaningful as the rate decision might be, it may be equally important to listen to Chair Warsh’s tone and commentary at the post-meeting press conference. There is still much for investors to learn about how the new chair will lead the central bank in the months ahead and throughout his term.",
